v1.5.3: 2026-10-07
	* Fixed default tag-mode resolution for tagged SEQUENCE OF and SET OF
	  elements. References to already-tagged CHOICE types now use IMPLICIT
	  tagging, as required by X.680:2021 §31.2.7. Added issue #566 regression
	  coverage for normalized ASN.1 and generated member descriptors.
	* Corrected IMPORTS resolution and diagnostics. Explicitly imported names
	  resolve from the module named by FROM; -fprefer-import-source disables
	  the legacy whole-module fallback. Duplicate module references are
	  diagnosed, OID equality checks avoid treating name-form arcs as numbers,
	  parameterized imported types avoid spurious diagnostics, and all FATAL
	  diagnostics produce a non-zero exit status. Added compiler regression
	  coverage (PR #560 follow-up).
	* Fixed PER extensibility handling for information-object identifier fields
	  governed by object sets and for component-relation constraints. Recovery
	  is limited to table-only constraints where appropriate. Added UPER and
	  APER regression coverage for issue #563 (PR #564).
	* Fixed a parallel uninstall race in the skeleton build that could cause
	  make distcheck to fail (PR #564).
	* Prevented generated filenames from colliding with skeleton files on
	  case-insensitive filesystems by disambiguating matching names with an
	  asn1c_ prefix. Added a smoke test and documentation.
	* Moved constraint enums to file scope and made asn1p_constr.h
	  self-contained, so C++-based code analyzers can parse the declarations.
	* Updated and regenerated the usage guide and man page to match current
	  behavior, including the transfer-syntax API table and groff rendering.
	  Added Markdown lint and VS Code workspace settings.

Changes since v1.5.0:
	* Made the generated-constraint warning regression test compatible with
	  Automake's standard top_srcdir/top_builddir test environment.
	* Avoided redundant parentheses around standalone equality comparisons in
	  generated constraint checks, preventing Clang's -Wparentheses-equality
	  warning while retaining required grouping for compound expressions.
	* Hardened APER open-type decoding against undefined NULL-pointer arithmetic
	  when malformed input begins with a zero-length chunk.  Regression coverage
	  now exercises the corresponding aligned-PER vector in check-126.
	  Fix suggested by <shakespark@gmail.com> in <https://github.com/vlm/asn1c/pull/551>.
	* Generalized generated OER, UPER, and APER descriptor constraint-table
	  inheritance for typedef aliases by deriving codec slots from the terminal
	  ASN.1 type. 
	  Issue #552, reported by @zhouvlia, was already avoided for ENUMERATED aliases
	  by an earlier enum-specific branch in this fork; the new terminal-type rule
	  covers the remaining alias classes and the added UPER/APER regression locks
	  in the reported behavior and truncation safety.
	* Corrected generated UPER/APER CHOICE maps so conversions between declaration
	  order and canonical order use the right direction. Added canonical-order
	  regression coverage in check-561. Fix in PR #562, included in v1.5.2.
	  Problem and fix provided by Ruud Schramp.
	IMPORTANT UPGRADE NOTICE:
	* Decoding behavior for unknown extensions has changed from "fail" to
	  "skip/relay". Evaluate the impact on your application before upgrading;
	  define ASN_REJECT_UNKNOWN_EXTENSIONS when compiling the decoder skeletons
	  to restore the previous strict behavior. This change can affect input-
	  validation gates and protocol state machines that treated RC_FAIL as a
	  protocol error.
	  Compatibility warning contributed by <shakespark@gmail.com>.

	INTEROPERABILITY FIXES (vlm/asn1c PRs #539-#548 and #550):
	* Co-authored-by: libo <shakespark@gmail.com>
	* The original fixes were authored by @shakespark (this notice is placed
	  here upon his request).
	* Ported vlm/asn1c PR #550 so generated permitted-alphabet constraint
	  checks accept a buffer-less empty string without NULL-pointer arithmetic
	  and deterministically reject malformed values whose buffer is NULL while
	  their size is non-zero. Runtime regression coverage exercises both empty
	  representations plus malformed, in-alphabet, and out-of-alphabet values;
	  generated permitted-alphabet helpers now include complete doc-blocks.
	* Corrected UPER known-multiplier character strings with extensible SIZE
	  constraints to retain their effective permitted-alphabet width outside
	  the size root, as required by X.691:2021 sections 30.4 and 30.5.2.
	  Also corrected the section 30.5.4 direct-value boundary, supported
	  zero-bit single-character alphabets, and rejected length arithmetic
	  overflow before allocation. Regression test 550 covers exact root and
	  extension encodings, round trips, malformed alphabet values, forward
	  decoding, empty strings, and a following-field cursor check.
	* Corrected UPER/OER forward-compatible handling of unknown CHOICE and
	  ENUMERATED extensions, including lossless ENUMERATED relay and the
	  optional ASN_REJECT_UNKNOWN_EXTENSIONS strict compatibility mode.
	* Corrected UPER normally-small long-form encoding, extensible constraint
	  construction, DEFAULT extension omission, SET canonical ordering, and
	  ENUMERATED automatic numbering/map layout.
	* Corrected OER open-type skipping to consume both its length determinant
	  and content, and added regression schemas and runtime tests for malformed,
	  truncated, boundary, cross-version, and canonical-encoding cases.
	* PR #539's 24-bit open-type skip defect was not present in this fork: its
	  existing bit-at-a-time skipper already consumed every payload length. The
	  upstream regression test was retained to lock in that behavior.
	* Fixed codec-disabled builds of NativeEnumerated by applying the UPER
	  extension-range consistency check only when the UPER limit constant is
	  available. This restores the all-codecs-disabled smoke-test variant.
	* Fixed generated UPER projects to include constr_SET_uper.c, and hardened
	  non-empty SET OF / SEQUENCE OF decoding against missing element codecs.
	  Empty collections remain valid because they do not invoke an element
	  codec.
	* Corrected PER-visible extensible SIZE roots so named extension additions
	  are excluded from the root while remaining accepted by runtime constraint
	  checks. Plain BIT STRING values below an extensible root are encoded as
	  extensions instead of being padded into a different abstract value.
	* Routed NamedBitList-specific BIT STRING descriptors through top-level
	  aliases and inline members, including compound-name output, while plain
	  BIT STRING values continue to preserve trailing zero bits.

	SECURITY FIXES:
	* Hardened APER constrained INTEGER decoding for ranges wider than 16 bits.
	  The decoder now rejects constraint metadata wider than its uintmax_t
	  accumulator and invalid values from the rounded constrained length
	  determinant before alignment or payload consumption.  Offset accumulation
	  remains unsigned and checks for shift overflow, preventing signed-shift
	  undefined behavior and over-long encodings that could desynchronize later
	  fields.  Added regression coverage for the reported 33-bit/8-octet input
	  and the 64-bit boundary path.
	* Hardened variable-size JER BIT STRING decoding.  The decoder now requires
	  the X.697 "value" and "length" members exactly once, rejects unknown or
	  trailing members, and does not assign a first- or last-member winner to
	  duplicate JSON names.  This prevents duplicate-member parser differentials
	  from silently changing the decoded bit string across implementations.
	  X.697 clause 24.3 defines the two required members but does not define a
	  duplicate-name resolution rule; RFC 8259 section 4 recommends unique names
	  and documents duplicate-name behavior as unpredictable.
	* Fixed generated OPEN TYPE selector code for Information Object Sets
	  whose rows define the selected open type but omit the constraining
	  key field.  The generated selector now validates both the constraining
	  cell and selected type cell before dereferencing type descriptors or
	  compare callbacks, preventing NULL dereferences on malicious input.
	  OPEN TYPE encoder and printer paths were also hardened to reject NULL
	  selected descriptors before debug logging, encoding, or printing.
	  Regression test 211 now covers the crash packet pattern and
	  BER/DER/OER/UPER/APER/XER/JER/CBOR round trips plus plaintext
	  printing through the same selector edge case.
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: low)
	* Hardened CVE-2025-32893 handling for parameterized Information Object
	  Sets by safely comparing VALUESET constraint references without
	  dereferencing optional constraint fields, and added regression test 212
	  to verify distinct value sets produce distinct open-type validation.
	  (Severity: medium; Security impact: medium)
	* Fixed CBOR unknown-field skipping so recursive arrays, maps, and tags
	  are covered by the decoder stack limit.  SEQUENCE and SET decoders use
	  the new cbor_skip_item_with_ctx() helper when skipping unknown CBOR
	  map values; the original cbor_skip_item() remains as a compatibility
	  wrapper for callers without decoder context.  Added check-CBOR
	  regression coverage for deeply nested tag wrappers.
	  (Severity: medium; Security impact: low)
	* Fixed BER CHOICE decoding infinite loop on malformed indefinite-length
	  end-of-contents (CWE-835, DoS on attacker-controlled input).  A leading
	  0x00 byte followed by a non-zero byte fell through an unhandled branch
	  in constr_CHOICE_ber.c without returning or advancing the buffer,
	  causing the decoder to spin forever.  The missing branch now returns
	  RC_FAIL, matching constr_SEQUENCE_ber.c / constr_SET_ber.c /
	  constr_SET_OF_ber.c behavior.  Added regression test
	  (203-ber-indef-loop-OK.asn1, check-203.c) covering all four
	  indefinite-length BER decoders, plus a libFuzzer harness and seed
	  corpus (data-203).  Ported from upstream vlm/asn1c PR #518; originally
	  reported by John Bradley (Credex).
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: low)

	FIXES:
	* Reduced randomized sanitizer CI compile time by applying each case's
	  ASN1_TEXT definition only to random-test-driver.o. Shared generated codec
	  objects now have stable command lines that ccache can reuse across bundle
	  cases. Standard CI explicitly disables the opt-in LibFuzzer mode and caps
	  every ordinary CI job, as well as each make-check step, at 40 minutes.
	* Restored the X.691 section 13.2.6 constrained length determinant
	  for APER constrained INTEGER values whose range is greater than
	  65536.  A previous fix for wide INTEGER constraint handling changed
	  this path to the general APER length determinant, producing and
	  expecting non-conformant encodings such as 01 20 instead of 00 20
	  for INTEGER (0..4294967295) ::= 32.  The decoder and encoder now
	  use the constrained len-1 bit field followed by octet alignment
	  while preserving the unsigned offset accumulation and negative lower
	  bound checks needed for 64-bit ranges.
	* Fixed tests/tests-asn1c-compiler subdirectory checks so they build
	  asn1c before running scripts that invoke it.  This prevents
	  check-parsing.sh from comparing references against empty output when
	  the compiler has not already been built by a top-level make.
	* Fixed Darwin libtool configuration when `sysctl -n kern.argmax` is
	  denied by the host environment.  configure now seeds libtool's command
	  line length cache from `getconf ARG_MAX`, avoiding empty max_cmd_len
	  values and noisy "integer expression expected" diagnostics while
	  linking skeleton archives.
	* Ported upstream OPEN TYPE and option validation fixes.  Decoders now
	  reject information object rows whose selector has no type descriptor
	  instead of dereferencing NULL, and OER OPEN TYPE failure cleanup resets
	  the OPEN TYPE CHOICE wrapper instead of using the selected primitive
	  type size.  Added regression test 211 for typeless information object
	  rows and truncated OPEN TYPE payloads.  The compiler now rejects
	  -fno-constraints with -gen-OER, -gen-UPER, or -gen-APER because those
	  encoders/decoders require constraint metadata.
	* Fixed additional fuzzer-discovered decoder issues:
	  - JER BIT STRING now rejects invalid length metadata instead of
	    accepting lengths larger than the decoded bit buffer or with more
	    than seven unused bits.
	  - APER SEQUENCE frees extension presence maps on starvation paths.
	  - APER NativeReal and OCTET STRING reject malformed length/range
	    cases found by fuzzing.
	  - JER and XER SET OF decoding now treats zero-progress member decodes
	    as failure, preventing loops on malformed input.
	  - The JER decoder and randomized/fuzzer test runners now handle
	    malformed or truncated inputs without writing discoveries back into
	    source-tree corpora.
	* Fixed XER OCTET STRING entity-reference handling so Unicode U+0000 is
	  accepted while out-of-range and surrogate numeric character references
	  fail cleanly with a terminated working buffer.
	* Keyed the single definition of `asn_debug_indent` in asn_internal.c
	  off a macro (ASN__DEBUG_INDENT_NEEDS_DEFINITION) set by asn_internal.h
	  under exactly the configuration which declares the variable extern.
	  Previously the definition's guard did not account for an external
	  ASN_DEBUG override, so building with -DASN_EMIT_DEBUG=1 plus a custom
	  -DASN_DEBUG=... failed to compile asn_internal.c.  Aligned with
	  upstream vlm/asn1c PR #520.
	* tests: instrument generated codec libraries with libFuzzer coverage
	  counters (-fsanitize=fuzzer-no-link) so fuzzing gets feedback from the
	  ASN.1 codec itself, and seed fuzzer runs from a scratch corpus copy so
	  discoveries are not written back into the source tree.  Ported from
	  upstream vlm/asn1c PR #518.

	NEW FEATURES:
	* Added schema-level XER/JER encoding instruction support for the
	  implemented subset of X.693/X.697-style controls.  The parser now
	  accepts `JER INSTRUCTIONS`, `[TEXT]`, `[XER:TEXT]`, `[DECIMAL]`,
	  `[XER:DECIMAL]`, `[JER:BASE64]`, `ENCODING-CONTROL XER` directives
	  for `TEXT`, `DECIMAL`, and `GLOBAL-DEFAULTS MODIFIED-ENCODINGS`, and
	  `ENCODING-CONTROL JER` directives for `BASE64`, enumerated-value
	  `TEXT AS`, and member `NAME AS`.
	  - Added semantic validation for target applicability, unknown targets,
	    required `AS` values, XER `DECIMAL` requiring
	    `GLOBAL-DEFAULTS MODIFIED-ENCODINGS`, and duplicate JER wire names.
	  - Added generated XER text wrappers for BOOLEAN, ENUMERATED,
	    named-number INTEGER, and named-bit BIT STRING; XER decimal REAL
	    routing; JER Base64 OCTET STRING wrappers; and JER member wire-name
	    metadata used by SEQUENCE, SET, and CHOICE encoders/decoders.
	  - Preserved compatibility for bare `[BASE64]` as XER and the legacy
	    XER OCTET STRING `hexadecimal`, `base64`, and `utf8` control forms.
	  - Added compiler golden and smoke tests covering allowed forms, bad
	    values, bad applicability, exact XER/JER output, JER round trips, and
	    JER bad-wire failures.
	* Added `-fprefer-import-source` compiler flag.  When two modules export
	  identically-named types and a consumer imports one from each,
	  `asn1f_lookup_in_imports` previously fell back to a full-module body
	  scan and silently bound to the wrong module's definition.  With
	  `-fprefer-import-source` the resolver only accepts an explicit
	  IMPORTS-list match, eliminating the ambiguity.  The fix also corrects
	  flag propagation through `_ex` wrapper functions and across the
	  `memset` that clears `a1f_replace_me_with_proper_interface_arg`, so
	  compiler-phase lookups now correctly inherit caller-supplied flags.

1.3.6:
	FIXES:
	* Initialize `char ch` before taking its address in
	  asn_codecs_prim_xer.c and asn_codecs_prim_jer.c to silence
	  clang -Werror,-Wuninitialized-const-pointer. Reported by ur20980.

1.3.5:
	FIXES:
	* Prevent unsigned underflow in APER constrained INTEGER decoding when
	  reading length-octets for ranges wider than 16 bits. The decoder now
	  rejects zero-length determinants and avoids size_t wraparound flagged
	  by UBSan on macOS builds. Reported by mouse07410.
	* Fixed check-fprefix-link.sh smoke test to ensure proper option
	  ordering for macOS compatibility. The test now places all command-line
	  options before the input file, avoiding POSIX getopt() behavior where
	  option processing stops at the first non-option argument.

1.3.4:
	NEW FEATURES:
	* Added CBOR tag support (RFC 8949 §3.4, major type 6).
	  - All CBOR decoders are now tag-transparent: any number of leading
	    tag headers are silently skipped before decoding the underlying
	    value.  Tagged data from external producers (self-described CBOR
	    tag 55799, epoch timestamps tag 1, URI hints tag 32, etc.) is
	    accepted without application-level changes.
	  - New cbor_skip_tags() helper in cbor_support.[ch] peels off
	    consecutive leading CBOR tag headers from a raw buffer.
	  - Added well-known CBOR tag constants to cbor_support.h:
	    CBOR_TAG_DATETIME_STRING (0), CBOR_TAG_EPOCH_DATETIME (1),
	    CBOR_TAG_DECIMAL_FRACTION (4), CBOR_TAG_BIGFLOAT (5),
	    CBOR_TAG_BASE64URL (21), CBOR_TAG_BASE64 (22), CBOR_TAG_BASE16 (23),
	    CBOR_TAG_ENCODED_CBOR (24), CBOR_TAG_URI (32), CBOR_TAG_REGEX (35),
	    CBOR_TAG_UUID (37), CBOR_TAG_NETWORK_ADDR (260),
	    CBOR_TAG_SELF_DESCRIBED (55799).
	  - Extended check-CBOR test suite with comprehensive tag tests:
	    cbor_encode_tag() output verification, cbor_skip_tags() unit tests,
	    tag-transparent decode tests for INTEGER, OCTET STRING, NativeInteger,
	    and BIT STRING types, and nested multi-tag decode tests.
	  - Updated asn1c-usage.tex: added "CBOR Tags" API section documenting
	    encoding with cbor_encode_tag(), tag-transparent decoding, and
	    bignum tags. Added IANA CBOR Tags Registry reference.
	    Updated CBOR references from RFC 7049 to RFC 8949 (successor).
	  - Updated asn1c.man.md: added CBOR TAGS section and updated RFC
	    reference from RFC 7049 to RFC 8949.
	FIXES:
	* Fixed generated filename collisions with system headers on
	  case-insensitive filesystems (notably macOS/Windows). ASN.1 types
	  whose generated filenames match common system headers are now
	  disambiguated automatically (e.g., Time.h -> asn1c_time.h),
	  preventing accidental inclusion of generated headers when source
	  files include <time.h>. Added smoke-test coverage for the Time case.

1.3.3:
	NEW FEATURES:
	* Added complete CBOR (Concise Binary Object Representation, RFC 7049)
	  codec support. CBOR generation is enabled by default; use -no-gen-CBOR
	  to disable. New skeleton files: cbor_encoder.[ch], cbor_decoder.[ch],
	  cbor_support.[ch], INTEGER_cbor.c, NativeInteger_cbor.c,
	  OCTET_STRING_cbor.c, BIT_STRING_cbor.c, BOOLEAN_cbor.c, NULL_cbor.c,
	  ENUMERATED_cbor.c, NativeEnumerated_cbor.c, REAL_cbor.c,
	  NativeReal_cbor.c, constr_SEQUENCE_cbor.c, constr_SEQUENCE_OF_cbor.c,
	  constr_SET_cbor.c, constr_SET_OF_cbor.c, constr_CHOICE_cbor.c,
	  asn_codecs_prim_cbor.c. The SEQUENCE encoder correctly skips absent
	  optional and default-valued members so the CBOR map header count always
	  matches the number of encoded key/value pairs. INTEGER decoding handles
	  CBOR bignum tags (2 and 3) for values exceeding the 64-bit signed range.
	  New test: tests/tests-skeletons/check-CBOR.c with edge-case coverage for
	  INTEGER, NativeInteger, BIT STRING, and OCTET STRING types.
	* Added ATS_CBOR to asn_transfer_syntax enum and wired CBOR encode/decode
	  into asn_encode()/asn_decode() dispatch in asn_application.c. Added
	  -icbor and -ocbor switches to converter-example.c so that generated
	  converter applications can read and write CBOR-encoded data.

1.3.2:
	FIXES:
	* Fixed incorrect type descriptor selection when the same member name appears
	  in different parent types with different type definitions. When embedded types
	  like ssb-PositionsInBurst appeared as CHOICE in one parent and SEQUENCE in 
	  another, the decoder would incorrectly use the wrong type descriptor due to
	  unsuffixed alias collisions at runtime. The fix ensures member table references
	  always use suffixed type descriptors for embedded constructed types, avoiding
	  ambiguity. Affects 3GPP RRC and similar specifications with duplicate member
	  names across different parent structures.
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Moved complex_threshold from global variable to arg_t structure field.
	  Applications linking to libasn1compiler no longer need to define their own
	  version of the global complex_threshold variable. The variable is now properly
	  encapsulated within the compiler's argument structure and passed through the
	  asn1_compile() function. Default threshold value remains 4. Added test case
	  for -fcomplex-threshold flag validation.
	  (Severity: low; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed JER OPEN TYPE decoder to comply with ITU-T X.697 Clause 41. The decoder
	  was incorrectly attempting to parse CHOICE-style key wrappers and consuming
	  parent SEQUENCE delimiters, causing "Unexpected JSON key" and "Out of defined
	  members" errors when decoding valid ITU-T X.697 compliant JSON. The decoder now
	  decodes OPEN TYPE values directly without wrapper parsing and returns immediately
	  without consuming trailing delimiters, letting parent decoders handle structural
	  elements. Added automated regression test to prevent future issues. Affects F1AP
	  and similar specifications with OPEN TYPE fields. (PR #456)
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: none)

1.3.1:
	FEATURES:
	* Enhanced -fprefix implementation with automatic PDU handling and system
	  header conflict warnings. (PR #427)
	* Added warning system to detect filename conflicts with system headers on
	  case-insensitive filesystems. (PR #425)

	NOTABLE:
	* Added S1AP missing ASN.1 file to examples. (PR #423)

	FIXES:
	* Improved JER OPEN_TYPE encoder validation and diagnostics. Added comprehensive
	  checks for type descriptor validity, NULL pointer detection, and type mismatch
	  warnings. Enhanced debug logging to help diagnose encoding issues in complex
	  IOC scenarios. (Severity: low; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed name collision for nested CHOICE/SET members with identical identifiers.
	  When the same identifier appears recursively in nested CHOICE or SET structures
	  (e.g., "criticalExtensions" used at multiple nesting levels in 3GPP RRC schemas),
	  the compiler now automatically applies compound naming to prevent collisions.
	  This fixes UPER decoding failures in 3GPP WCDMA RRC and similar schemas.
	  (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed JER Open Type encoding to comply with ITU-T X.697 Clause 41 - removed
	  incorrect type name wrapper. (PR #444) (Severity: medium; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed SEQUENCE OF with inline SEQUENCE inside CHOICE generating undefined
	  types. (PR #442) (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed linker errors from duplicate unsuffixed type descriptor symbols on
	  non-ELF platforms (CYGWIN, Windows). (PR #439) (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed duplicate validation function names for nested ENUMERATEDs with
	  identical identifiers. (PR #436) (Severity: high; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed parser memory leak on syntax error. (PR #434) (Severity: low; Security impact: low)
	* Fixed memory leak in parser when processing unused tokens. (PR #433)
	  (Severity: low; Security impact: low)
	* Fixed code generation for deeply nested SEQUENCE OF with compound names.
	  (PR #432) (Severity: medium; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed XER Base64 decoder state loss in chunked decoding. (PR #430)
	  (Severity: medium; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed time.h shadowing on case-insensitive filesystems (macOS, Windows) by
	  moving include to header files. (PR #425) (Severity: medium; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed XER encoder indentation and empty element spacing issues. (PR #420)
	  (Severity: low; Security impact: none)
	* Fixed unused variable 'er' in OPEN_TYPE_jer.c that caused compilation
	  failure with -Werror -Wall flags. (Severity: low; Security impact: none)

